      "In 1916, they returned to England while the husband was on leave.",
      "The wife was suffering from rheumatoid arthritis, and her doctor advised her to remain in England for some time.",
      "Before returning to Ceylon, the husband orally promised to pay her £30 per month until she joined him.",
      "Later, differences arose between the couple, and the wife filed a case to recover the promised monthly amount.",
      "The husband argued that the promise was a domestic arrangement and was never intended to create a legally enforceable contract."
